'''''Echium nervosum''''' is a species of flowering plants of the family [[Boraginaceae]].<ref name="Tropicos">{{cite web|url=http://www.tropicos.org/Name/4002880|title=Echium nervosum|publisher=Tropicos|accessdate=2018-03-08}}</ref> It is endemic to [[Madeira]].<ref name="IPNI">{{IPNI| id = 115792-1 | taxon = Echium nervosum | accessdate = 28 January 2019}}</ref> The specific name ''nervosum'' is from Latin and means "veined".<ref>[http://www.winternet.com/~chuckg/dictionary/dictionary.126.html Dictionary of Botanical Epithets]</ref>

==Description==
It is a compact woody shrub, average height {{convert|100|cm}}, maximum height {{convert|150|cm}}. The leaves are narrow, densely haired and silver green. Its flowers are pale blue to pale bluish rose and sit in an egg-shaped inflorescence.<ref name="rareplants">{{cite web|url=http://www.rareplants.de/shop/product.asp?P_ID=6538|title=Echium nervosum|publisher=Rareplants|accessdate=28 January 2019}}</ref>

